&lt;h3&gt;Burn Ban&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;May 15, 2026 - No wood or charcoal fires are allowed. You may cook with containerized fuel stoves (i.e. propane).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Phones Down&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oct. 9, 2026 - Phones are down in the park.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Road Closure&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source='MessageBody'&gt;Oct. 29, 2026 - The access road to the CCC restroom is closed for maintenance. The restrooms remain open but can only be accessed by walking.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Water Contaminant Notice&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oct. 9, 2026 - The park uses water provided by the City of Big Spring. The city has issued a notice that its water exceeds 'Maximum Containment Level' of trihalomethanes. &lt;a href='https://www.mybigspring.com/DocumentCenter/View/38357/Maximum-Contaminant-TTHM-Level-Violation-6-2-26' data-linktype='external' data-val='https://www.mybigspring.com/DocumentCenter/View/38357/Maximum-Contaminant-TTHM-Level-Violation-6-2-26'&gt;Learn more about this contaminant on the city's website&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check back for updates.&lt;/p&gt;

