&lt;h3&gt;Low Lake Level&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;June 22, 2026 - Buescher's lake is lower than normal. There is no view of or access to the lake from the cabins or from the Oak Haven and Lakeview campgrounds. Fishing is still available at the day-use picnic and canoe launch areas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check back for updates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Boat Ramp and Canoe Rental Closure&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oct. 21, 2026 - The canoe rentals and boat ramp are closed due to extremely low water levels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check back for updates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Bison Safety&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;July 27, 2026 - During rutting season (May through September), use extra caution around bison. Never stand between a bull and cows and always&amp;nbsp;stay at least 50 yards away for your safety.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Lake Closures&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;April 10, 2026 - The boat ramp, fishing pier and swimming area are closed due to the low lake level. Swimming is still allowed in the lake.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Park Closures&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The park will be closed on the following dates:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 p.m. on Dec. 7 to 2 p.m. Dec. 11&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 p.m. on Dec. 14 to 2 p.m. Dec. 18&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 p.m. on Dec. 18 to 2 p.m. Dec. 23&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Only permitted hunters will be allowed on these dates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Water Quality Advisory&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oct. 21, 2025 - The park has detected higher than normal nitrate levels in its water system. Infants under 6 months, pregnant women, and people with specific health concerns should plan on bringing water when visiting the park.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note&lt;/strong&gt;: Boiling water does not remove nitrates.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check back for updates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Visiting the Park&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We recommend &lt;a href='https://texasstateparks.reserveamerica.com/cedar-hill-state-park/r/facilityDetails.do?contractCode=TX&amp;amp;parkId=1200114&amp;amp;_ga=2.267879694.1622435341.1672668084-242518747.1667330383' data-linktype='external' data-val='https://texasstateparks.reserveamerica.com/cedar-hill-state-park/r/facilityDetails.do?contractCode=TX&amp;amp;parkId=1200114&amp;amp;_ga=2.267879694.1622435341.1672668084-242518747.1667330383'&gt;reserving day passes&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for weekends and holidays. If your plans change, please modify or cancel your reservation so someone else can visit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trails close for wet weather and maintenance. Check &lt;a data-val='f0405383b77d4afd9b12abf98b1af9c2' href='https://tpwd.texas.gov/state-parks/park-information/notices/cedar-hill-alert-promo' data-linktype='internal'&gt;current trail status&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;before visiting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a data-val='258daaba53dc4817a6dc6995927b39fb' href='https://tpwd.texas.gov/state-parks/park-information/wildlife/invasive-ants' data-linktype='internal'&gt;Argentine ants&lt;/a&gt; have been identified in some of our campsites. These invasive ants do not sting. Be prepared to treat around your vehicle and camping equipment. Texas Parks and Wildlife Department is working to reduce the number of ants without harming the park's natural resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check back for updates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Park Closure&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;June 1, 2026 - The park is closed for development. An opening date has not been set.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check back for updates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Screwworm Alert&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href='https://tpwd.texas.gov/huntwild/wild/diseases/screwworm/' data-linktype='external' data-val='https://tpwd.texas.gov/huntwild/wild/diseases/screwworm/'&gt;New world screwworm &lt;/a&gt;has been found in parts of Texas.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Check your pets and livestock often.&lt;/strong&gt; If you see unusual wounds or maggots, &lt;strong&gt;do not move the animal&lt;/strong&gt;. Call the Texas Animal Health Commission at (800) 550‑8242 or contact a private veterinarian.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For &lt;strong&gt;wildlife&lt;/strong&gt; with suspicious wounds or maggots, notify park staff or call (512) 389‑4505.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Boating Notices&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;July 26, 2026 - Due to lake levels:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exercise extreme caution when operating watercraft on the lake due to current Frio River conditions at the 99 and Mason Point boat ramps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You may launch below the concrete ramp when conditions are safe. Please watch for debris in the water and launch at your own risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The following boat ramps are currently open:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calliham&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;South Shore&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mason Point&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hwy. 99&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Unit Closures&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The South Shore unit will be closed on the following dates:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 p.m. on Nov. 30 to 10 p.m. on Dec. 3&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Calliham unit will be closed on the following dates:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5p.m. on Jan. 4 to 10 p.m. Jan. 8&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Only permitted hunters will be allowed on these dates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check back for updates or contact the park for more information.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Screwworm Alert&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href='https://tpwd.texas.gov/huntwild/wild/diseases/screwworm/' data-linktype='external' data-val='https://tpwd.texas.gov/huntwild/wild/diseases/screwworm/'&gt;New world screwworm &lt;/a&gt;has been found in parts of Texas.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Check your pets and livestock often.&lt;/strong&gt; If you see unusual wounds or maggots, &lt;strong&gt;do not move the animal&lt;/strong&gt;. Call the Texas Animal Health Commission at (800) 550‑8242 or contact a private veterinarian.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For &lt;strong&gt;wildlife&lt;/strong&gt; with suspicious wounds or maggots, notify park staff or call (512) 389‑4505.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span data-ogsc='black'&gt;&lt;span class='mark1qh55xz9j' data-markjs='true' data-ogac='' data-ogab='' data-ogsc='' data-ogsb='' data-ogsbtc='' data-ogsbrc='' data-ogsbbc='' data-ogsblc='' data-olk-copy-source='MessageBody'&gt;Holiday&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class='markx800977df' data-markjs='true' data-ogac='' data-ogab='' data-ogsc='' data-ogsb='' data-ogsbtc='' data-ogsbrc='' data-ogsbbc='' data-ogsblc=''&gt;Hours&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ogsc='black'&gt;The park will remain open throughout the &lt;span class='mark1qh55xz9j' data-markjs='true' data-ogac='' data-ogab='' data-ogsc='' data-ogsb='' data-ogsbtc='' data-ogsbrc='' data-ogsbbc='' data-ogsblc=''&gt;holiday&lt;/span&gt;s. The office will be closed during the following times:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-ogsc='black'&gt;Thanksgiving Day, Nov. 26: closed all day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-ogsc='black'&gt;Christmas Eve, Dec. 24: closing at noon&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-ogsc='black'&gt;Christmas Day, Dec. 25: closed all day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Park Closures&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The park will be closed on the following dates:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 p.m. on Oct. 19 to 2 p.m. Oct. 22&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 p.m. on Nov. 5 to 2 p.m. Nov. 8&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 p.m. on Nov. 16 to 2 p.m. Nov. 19&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 p.m. on Dec. 3 to 2 p.m. Dec. 6&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 p.m. on Dec. 14 to 2 p.m. Dec. 17&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Only permitted hunters will be allowed on these dates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Visiting the Park&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Carry water when hiking:&lt;/strong&gt; Carry plenty of water for you, your family and your pets when hiking. Experts recommend one liter of water per person per hour of activity, no matter the temperature.&amp;nbsp;Many of our trails are rocky and unshaded. Water spigots are available in the campground.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reservations recommended:&lt;/strong&gt; We highly recommend making day pass or camping reservations before visiting to guarantee entry.&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href='https://texasstateparks.reserveamerica.com/colorado-bend-state-park/r/facilityDetails.do?contractCode=TX&amp;amp;parkId=1200055&amp;amp;pk_vid=ce5f07833a242ae81739934896bb32ea'&gt;Reserve online&lt;/a&gt; or by calling (512) 389-8900.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check back for updates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Burn Bans&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nov. 6, 2026 - The South Sulphur Unit is under a burn ban. No wood fires are allowed. &lt;span data-olk-copy-source='MessageBody'&gt;Propane or containerized fuels may be used for cooking only. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Boat Ramp Notice&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nov. 6, 2025 - The Honey Creek boat ramp at the South Sulphur unit is closed due to the low lake level. The boat ramps at South Sulphur in Gulls Bluff, the Tira Satellite boat ramp, and Lone Pine boat ramp at&amp;nbsp;Doctors Creek Unit remain open.&amp;nbsp;Please be aware of low lake levels and use caution at the boat ramps.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Trail Alert&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trails close to horseback riders after rainfall. Check conditions before you come by calling the park.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Park Closures&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The entire park will be closed on the following dates:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10 p.m. Jan. 8 to 8 a.m. Jan. 11&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Coyote Run trail at the South Sulphur unit will be closed (but equestrian trails will remain open):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10 p.m. Dec. 4 to 8 a.m. Dec. 21&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Only permitted hunters will be allowed on these dates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contact the park for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check back for updates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Burn Ban&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nov. 11, 2025 - The park is under a burn ban. No wood or charcoal fires are allowed. You may cook with containerized fuel stoves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Headquarters Closure&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Park headquarters is closed on Monday, Oct. 26, 2026. Please use the self-pay station.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Facility Closures&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sept. 9, 2025 - The boat ramp and fishing pier are closed due to low lake level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Drought Notice&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;July 18, 2025 - This area is under Stage 4 water restrictions. Please use water wisely when you visit. Consider bringing water with you.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Park Closures&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The park will be closed on the following dates:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Noon on Nov. 13 to 8 a.m. Nov. 16&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Noon on Dec. 4 to 8 a.m. Dec. 7&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Noon on Dec. 18 to 8 a.m. Dec. 21&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Noon on Jan. 8 to 8 a.m. Jan. 11&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Only permitted hunters will be allowed on these dates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contact the park for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check back for updates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source='MessageBody'&gt;Holiday Hours&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The park will remain open throughout the holidays. The office will be closed during the following times:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thanksgiving Day, Nov. 26: closing at noon&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Christmas Eve, Dec. 24: closing at noon&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Christmas Day, Dec. 25: closed all day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check back for updates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Screwworm Notice&lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;The park is within an infested zone for the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href='https://tpwd.texas.gov/huntwild/wild/diseases/screwworm/' rel='noopener noreferrer' target='_blank' title='https://tpwd.texas.gov/huntwild/wild/diseases/screwworm/' data-auth='NotApplicable' data-linkindex='2' data-ogsc=''&gt;new world screwworm&lt;/a&gt;. For the safety of animals and to prevent the spread of this dangerous pest:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol start='1' type='1'&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Horse inspection may be required before leaving the park.&amp;nbsp; Please call park headquarters before visiting to ask about TAHC requirements and schedule an inspection.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;If you bring pets, inspect them daily for cuts, wounds and signs of infestation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span&gt;If you see animals with unusual wounds or maggots, do not move them.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;Let someone know where you saw them:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol start='3' type='1'&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span&gt;For pets/livestock&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span&gt;: Contact park staff or the Animal Health Commission at (737) 900-7455.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span&gt;For wildlife&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span&gt;: Contact park staff or call (512) 389-4505.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Burn Ban&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Jan. 1, 2026 - No wood fires are allowed. However, charcoal and containerized fuel stoves (i.e. propane) are allowed for cooking.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Primitive Area Closures&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The primitive camping area will be closed on the following dates:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6 a.m. on Oct. 2 to 8 a.m. on Oct. 10&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6 a.m. on Nov. 6 to 8 a.m. on Nov. 11&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6 a.m. on Feb. 19 to 8 a.m. on Feb. 24&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Only permitted hunters will be allowed on these dates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contact the park for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check back for updates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Park Closed&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nov. 9, 2026 - The&amp;nbsp;Del Norte Unit is closed due to flooding on Dolan Creek Rd. The unit will reopen on Friday, Nov. 13 following the regular Tuesday-Thursday closures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Screwworm Alert&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nov. 4, 2026 -&amp;nbsp;The park is within an infested zone for the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href='https://tpwd.texas.gov/huntwild/wild/diseases/screwworm/' rel='noopener noreferrer' target='_blank' title='https://tpwd.texas.gov/huntwild/wild/diseases/screwworm/'&gt;new world screwworm&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;For the safety of animals and to prevent the spread of this dangerous pest, please inspect pets daily for cuts, wounds and signs of infestation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you see animals with unusual wounds or maggots, do not move them.&amp;nbsp;Let someone know where you saw them:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For pets/livestock&lt;/strong&gt;: Contact park staff or the Animal Health Commission at (737) 900-7455.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For wildlife&lt;/strong&gt;: Contact park staff or call (512) 389-4505.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;No Potable Water&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;May 6, 2026 - Potable (drinkable) water is not available at the Del Norte Unit of the park. Bring water for drinking and cooking for your entire group when you visit.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Burn Ban&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Jan. 1, 2026 -&amp;nbsp;No wood fires allowed. You may cook with containerized fuels (i.e. propane).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Paddler Notices&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Jan. 1, 2026 - The Baker's Crossing launch is closed due to low flow levels in Devils River. The San Pedro Point launch is still open.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Unit Closures&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Dan A. Hughes unit will be closed on the following dates:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 p.m. on Nov. 16 to 8 a.m. on Nov. 27&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 p.m. on Dec. 7 to 8 a.m. on Dec. 18&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 p.m. on Jan. 11 to 8 a.m. on Jan. 22&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Del Norte unit will be closed on the following dates:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 p.m. on Nov. 30 to 8 a.m. on Dec. 11&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 p.m. on Dec. 14 to 8 a.m. on Dec. 25&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 p.m. on Jan. 4&amp;nbsp;to 8 a.m. on Jan. 15&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Only permitted hunters will be allowed on these dates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contact the park for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contact the park or check back for updates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Screwworm Alert&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href='https://tpwd.texas.gov/huntwild/wild/diseases/screwworm/' data-linktype='external' data-val='https://tpwd.texas.gov/huntwild/wild/diseases/screwworm/'&gt;New world screwworm &lt;/a&gt;has been found in parts of Texas.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Check your pets and livestock often.&lt;/strong&gt; If you see unusual wounds or maggots, &lt;strong&gt;do not move the animal&lt;/strong&gt;. Call the Texas Animal Health Commission at (800) 550‑8242 or contact a private veterinarian.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For &lt;strong&gt;wildlife&lt;/strong&gt; with suspicious wounds or maggots, notify park staff or call (512) 389‑4505.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

