&lt;h3&gt;Argentine Ants&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-val='258daaba53dc4817a6dc6995927b39fb' href='https://tpwd.texas.gov/state-parks/park-information/wildlife/invasive-ants' data-linktype='internal'&gt;Argentine ants&lt;/a&gt;, an invasive species, have been identified in some campsites in the park. The ants do not sting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Texas Parks and Wildlife Department is working with experts to reduce the ants without harming natural resources. Before leaving, thoroughly inspect your vehicle, RV, camping gear and other equipment; if you see the ants, please notify park staff immediately and they can offer guidance for treating. For park-specific questions, please contact the park at (903) 836-4336.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check back for updates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Burn Ban&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oct. 29, 2026 - The park is under a burn ban. No wood or charcoal fires are allowed&amp;nbsp;in the fire rings. For cooking, you may use wood smoker or pellet grills, propane or charcoal grills, cook stoves, griddles, or propane fire pits if they have a lid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Area Closures&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source='MessageBody'&gt;Sept. 18, 2026 - The boat ramp on the Hen House side of the park is closed. We expect it to reopen in the spring of 2027.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source='MessageBody'&gt;The 100 and 200 camping loops, restrooms and fish cleaning station at the Hen House Ridge Unit are closed for a construction project through February 2027.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Hen House day-use area remains open.&lt;/p&gt;
